     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock, and amlodipine's long half-life means the effects could last for days. Nothing you've told me about the patient (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify it. It may be a typo for 5 mg.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a licensed clinician with prescribing authority who is responsible for the patient. I can't enter an order on behalf of someone outside that role.\n\n**Next steps:**\n- Ask the treating clinician or prescriber on the medicine service to place the order.\n- If a prescriber confirms they want amlodipine at a standard dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, have them tell me the dose and I'll enter it.\n- If 50 mg was intentional, pharmacy or the attending physician should review it first."
      }
     ],
